{"book":{"id":"book-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell","slug":"the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell","title":"The Last Campaign: How Harry Truman Won the 1948 Election","authors":[{"id":"person-zachary-karabell","name":"Zachary Karabell"}],"isbn13":["9780375400865"],"subjects":["Biography"],"topics":["Cold War & Nuclear Politics","Democracy & Elections","Housing, Cities & Urban Life","Media, Journalism & Public Opinion"],"centralFigures":["Harry Truman","Thomas E. Dewey"],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=The%20Last%20Campaign%3A%20How%20Harry%20Truman%20Won%20the%201948%20Election%20Zachary%20Karabell","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=The%20Last%20Campaign%3A%20How%20Harry%20Truman%20Won%20the%201948%20Election%20Zachary%20Karabell","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=The%20Last%20Campaign%3A%20How%20Harry%20Truman%20Won%20the%201948%20Election%20Zachary%20Karabell","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=The%20Last%20Campaign%3A%20How%20Harry%20Truman%20Won%20the%201948%20Election%20Zachary%20Karabell","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL451877W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-heartland-nonfiction-wikipedia-chicago-tribune-heartland-prize","source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"],"readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.398,"accessibilityScore":0.109,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"narrative","score":0.68,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"story of\"","catalog text contains \"tells the story\"","catalog text contains \"quest\""]},{"id":"biographical","score":0.34,"confidence":"low","evidence":["biography subject or topic"]},{"id":"reported","score":0.34,"confidence":"low","evidence":["journalism/reportage subject or topic"]},{"id":"argument_driven","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"argues\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Harry Truman","confidence":0.9},{"name":"Thomas E. Dewey","confidence":0.72}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":false,"statement":"","confidence":0},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.35},"profileConfidence":0.72,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Henry Wallace","confidence":0.42}],"argument":{"statement":"Karabell argues that Truman’s 1948 victory depended on questionable political tactics, and that this victory came at great cost, paving the way for Republican backlash and 1950s anti-Communist crusades.","confidence":0.55}},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"6e3f91210551e9396f411cdaab112a131d96b59f84eb1dccd616f9e2f215c072","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"summary":"\"It was the last presidential campaign in which Americans truly had a choice across the ideological spectrum, from the far Right to the far Left. And the winner, according to pundits and pollsters alike, would be the Republican standard-bearer, Governor Thomas E. Dewey of New York. After sixteen years of Democratic rule, Americans seemed tired of the party and, in particular, of the somewhat inept incumbent, Harry Truman. Furthermore, Truman's chances appeared doomed by the growing strength of Henry Wallace's left-wing Progressive Party and Storm Thurmond's right-wing States' Rights Party, both drawing upon traditional Democratic constituencies.\". \"Zachary Karabell tells the story of all four campaigns. Karabell argues that 1948 was the last time a presidential race would be dominated by radio and print media, and the last time progressive and far-Left viewpoints were openly debated and covered in the mainstream press, before the Cold War consensus placed an entire spectrum of political views beyond the pale.\". \"Finally, Karabell shows why the polls were totally wrong, and how in the end Truman indulged in questionable political tactics to win the presidency. And he explains why this victory came at great cost to Truman's second term and to the country, paving the way for a Republican backlash and the virulent anti-Communist crusades of the 1950s.\"--BOOK JACKET.","publicationYear":2000,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Presidents","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Election","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Elections","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Verkiezingen","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Presidenten","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Truman, harry s., 1884-1972","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Presidents, united states, election, 1948","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Dewey, thomas e. (thomas edmund), 1902-1971","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell"}],"displaySummary":"And the in particular, of the somewhat inept incumbent, Harry Truman. Furthermore, Truman's chances appeared doomed by the growing strength of Henry Wallace's left-wing Progressive Party and Storm Thurmond's right-wing States' Rights Party, both drawing upon traditional Democratic constituencies.\". \"Zachary Karabell tells the story of all four campaigns. Karabell argues that 1948 was the last time a presidential race would be dominated by radio and print media, and the last time progressive and far-Left viewpoints were openly debated and covered in the mainstream press, before the Cold War consensus placed an entire spectrum of political views beyond the pale.\". \"Finally, Karabell shows why the polls were totally wrong, and how in the end Truman indulged in questionable political tactics to win the presidency. And he explains why this victory came at great cost to Truman's second term and to the country, paving the way for a Republican backlash and the virulent anti-Communist crusades of the 1950s.\"--BOOK JACKET.","primarySubject":"Biography","primaryTopic":"Cold War & Nuclear Politics","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Biography","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Biography","score":12,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Politics & Government","score":5,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Truman, harry s., 1884-1972","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell-2"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Dewey, thomas e. (thomas edmund), 1902-1971","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-last-campaign-how-harry-truman-won-the-1948-election-zachary-karabell","i